COPY bible.verse_text (verse_id, translation, text, license, attribution) FROM stdin;
Gen.1.1	KJV	In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.2	KJV	And the earth was without form, and void; and darkness was upon the face of the deep. And the Spirit of God moved upon the face of the waters.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.3	KJV	And God said, Let there be light: and there was light.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.4	KJV	And God saw the light, that it was good: and God divided the light from the darkness.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.5	KJV	And God called the light Day, and the darkness he called Night. And the evening and the morning were the first day.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.6	KJV	And God said, Let there be a firmament in the midst of the waters, and let it divide the waters from the waters.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.7	KJV	And God made the firmament, and divided the waters which were under the firmament from the waters which were above the firmament: and it was so.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.8	KJV	And God called the firmament Heaven. And the evening and the morning were the second day.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.9	KJV	And God said, Let the waters under the heaven be gathered together unto one place, and let the dry land appear: and it was so.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.10	KJV	And God called the dry land Earth; and the gathering together of the waters called he Seas: and God saw that it was good.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.11	KJV	And God said, Let the earth bring forth grass, the herb yielding seed, and the fruit tree yielding fruit after his kind, whose seed is in itself, upon the earth: and it was so.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.12	KJV	And the earth brought forth grass, and herb yielding seed after his kind, and the tree yielding fruit, whose seed was in itself, after his kind: and God saw that it was good.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.13	KJV	And the evening and the morning were the third day.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.14	KJV	And God said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.15	KJV	And let them be for lights in the firmament of the heaven to give light upon the earth: and it was so.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.16	KJV	And God made two great lights; the greater light to rule the day, and the lesser light to rule the night: he made the stars also.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.17	KJV	And God set them in the firmament of the heaven to give light upon the earth,	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.18	KJV	And to rule over the day and over the night, and to divide the light from the darkness: and God saw that it was good.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.19	KJV	And the evening and the morning were the fourth day.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.20	KJV	And God said, Let the waters bring forth abundantly the moving creature that hath life, and fowl that may fly above the earth in the open firmament of heaven.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.21	KJV	And God created great whales, and every living creature that moveth, which the waters brought forth abundantly, after their kind, and every winged fowl after his kind: and God saw that it was good.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.22	KJV	And God blessed them, saying, Be fruitful, and multiply, and fill the waters in the seas, and let fowl multiply in the earth.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.23	KJV	And the evening and the morning were the fifth day.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.24	KJV	And God said, Let the earth bring forth the living creature after his kind, cattle, and creeping thing, and beast of the earth after his kind: and it was so.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.25	KJV	And God made the beast of the earth after his kind, and cattle after their kind, and every thing that creepeth upon the earth after his kind: and God saw that it was good.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.26	KJV	And God said, Let us make man in our image, after our likeness: and let them have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over the cattle, and over all the earth, and over every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.27	KJV	So God created man in his own image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.28	KJV	And God blessed them, and God said unto them, Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth, and subdue it: and have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over every living thing that moveth upon the earth.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.29	KJV	And God said, Behold, I have given you every herb bearing seed, which is upon the face of all the earth, and every tree, in the which is the fruit of a tree yielding seed; to you it shall be for meat.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.30	KJV	And to every beast of the earth, and to every fowl of the air, and to every thing that creepeth upon the earth, wherein there is life, I have given every green herb for meat: and it was so.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.1.31	KJV	And God saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good. And the evening and the morning were the sixth day.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.1	KJV	Thus the heavens and the earth were finished, and all the host of them.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.2	KJV	And on the seventh day God ended his work which he had made; and he rested on the seventh day from all his work which he had made.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.3	KJV	And God blessed the seventh day, and sanctified it: because that in it he had rested from all his work which God created and made.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.4	KJV	These are the generations of the heavens and of the earth when they were created, in the day that the LORD God made the earth and the heavens,	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.5	KJV	And every plant of the field before it was in the earth, and every herb of the field before it grew: for the LORD God had not caused it to rain upon the earth, and there was not a man to till the ground.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.6	KJV	But there went up a mist from the earth, and watered the whole face of the ground.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.7	KJV	And the LORD God formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.8	KJV	And the LORD God planted a garden eastward in Eden; and there he put the man whom he had formed.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.9	KJV	And out of the ground made the LORD God to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.10	KJV	And a river went out of Eden to water the garden; and from thence it was parted, and became into four heads.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.11	KJV	The name of the first is Pison: that is it which compasseth the whole land of Havilah, where there is gold;	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.12	KJV	And the gold of that land is good: there is bdellium and the onyx stone.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.13	KJV	And the name of the second river is Gihon: the same is it that compasseth the whole land of Ethiopia.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.14	KJV	And the name of the third river is Hiddekel: that is it which goeth toward the east of Assyria. And the fourth river is Euphrates.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.15	KJV	And the LORD God took the man, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
Gen.2.16	KJV	And the LORD God commanded the man, saying, Of every tree of the garden thou mayest freely eat:	Public Domain	King James Version via Theographic Bible Metadata
