baal-hazor_142	Baal-hazor	Baal-hazor	Baal-hazor	Baal-hazor	\N	City	\N	31.979434	35.279229	Theographic	31.979434	35.279229	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	1	2 Samuel 13:23	Having a courtyard, or Baal’s village, the place on the borders of Ephraim and Benjamin where Absalom held the feast of sheep-shearing when Amnon was assassinated (2 Sam. 13:23). Probably it is the same with Hazor (Neh. 11:33), now Tell’ Asur, 5 miles north-east of Bethel.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
