baal-zephon_149	Baal-zephon	Baal-zephon	Baal-zephon	Baal-zephon	\N	City	\N	29.938441	32.395473	Theographic	29.938441	32.395473	Rough	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	3	Exodus 14:2	Baal of the north, an Egyptian town on the shores of the Gulf of Suez (Ex. 14:2; Num. 33:7), over against which the children of Israel encamped before they crossed the Red Sea. It is probably to be identified with the modern Jebel Deraj or Kulalah, on the western shore of the Gulf of Suez. Baal-zapuna of the Egyptians was a place of worship.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
