beth-shemesh_234	Beth-shemesh	Beth-shemesh (city, 1 Chronicles 6:59)	Beth-shemesh	Beth-shemesh	\N	City	\N	31.73072	34.99293	Theographic	31.75274836	34.97660913	Unknown	Verified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	17	1 Chronicles 6:59	A sacerdotal city in the tribe of Dan (Josh. 21:16; 1 Sam. 6:15), on the north border of Judah (Josh. 15:10). It was the scene of an encounter between Jehoash, king of Israel, and Amaziah, king of Judah, in which the latter was made prisoner (2 Kings 14:11, 13). It was afterwards taken by the Philistines (2 Chr. 28:18). It is the modern ruined Arabic village ‘Ain-shems, on the north-west slopes of the mountains of Judah, 14 miles west of Jerusalem.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
