bethlehem_218	Bethlehem	Bethlehem (city, 1 Chronicles 11:16)	Bethlehem	Bethlehem	\N	City	\N	31.70431	35.20746	Theographic	31.70536129	35.2102663	Unknown	Verified	\N	\N	\N	Both	32	1 Chronicles 11:16	A city in the “hill country” of Judah. It was originally called Ephrath (Gen. 35:16, 19; 48:7; Ruth 4:11). It was also called Beth-lehem Ephratah (Micah 5:2), Beth-lehem-judah (1 Sam. 17:12), and “the city of David” (Luke 2:4). It is first noticed in Scripture as the place where Rachel died and was buried “by the wayside,” directly to the north of the city (Gen. 48:7). The valley to the east was the scene of the story of Ruth the Moabitess.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
