bethsaida_231	Bethsaida	Bethsaida	Bethsaida	Bethsaida	\N	City	\N	32.91031	35.63067	Theographic	32.90784828	35.62697296	Unknown	Verified	\N	\N	\N	New Testament	7	John 1:44	A city near which Christ fed 5,000 (Luke 9:10; comp. John 6:17; Matt. 14:15-21), and where the blind man had his sight restored (Mark 8:22), on the east side of the lake, two miles up the Jordan. It stood within the region of Gaulonitis, and was enlarged by Philip the tetrarch, who called it “Julias,” after the emperor’s daughter. Or, as some have supposed, there may have been but one Bethsaida built on both sides of the lake, near where the Jordan enters it.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
