carchemish_277	Carchemish	Carchemish	Carchemish	Carchemish	\N	City	\N	36.82928161	38.01576051	Theographic	36.82928161	38.01576051	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	3	2 Chronicles 35:20	Fortress of Chemosh, a city on the west bank of the Euphrates (Jer. 46:2; 2 Chr. 35:20), not, as was once supposed, the Circesium at the confluence of the Chebar and the Euphrates, but a city considerably higher up the river, and commanding the ordinary passage of the Euphrates; probably identical with Hierapolis. It was the capital of the kingdom of the northern Hittites.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
carmel_278	Carmel	Carmel	Carmel	Carmel	\N	City	\N	31.422876	35.132952	Theographic	31.43333152	35.13333189	Unknown	Verified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	22	1 Chronicles 11:37	A town in the hill country of Judah (Josh. 15:55), the residence of Nabal (1 Sam. 25:2, 5, 7, 40), and the native place of Abigail, who became David’s wife (1 Sam. 27:3). Here king Uzziah had his vineyards (2 Chr. 26:10). The ruins of this town still remain under the name of Kurmul, about 10 miles south-south-east of Hebron, close to those of Maon.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
