crete_310	Crete	Crete	Crete	Crete	\N	Island	\N	35.23102579604995	24.85162918	Theographic	35.171239	25.007204	Unknown	Verified	\N	\N	island	New Testament	5	Acts 27:12	Now called Candia, one of the largest islands in the Meditterranean, about 140 miles long and 35 broad. It was at one time a very prosperous and populous island, having a “hundred cities.” The character of the people is described in Paul’s quotation from “one of their own poets” (Epimenides) in his epistle to Titus: “The Cretans are alway liars, evil beasts, slow bellies” (Titus 1:12). Jews from Crete were in Jerusalem on the day of Pentecost (Acts 2:11).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
