cush_312	Cush	Cush	Cush	Cush	\N	Region	\N	21.959788	31.343557	Theographic	21.959788	31.343557	Related-Surrounding	Not identifiable	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	16	2 Kings 19:9	A son, probably the eldest, of Ham, and the father of Nimrod (Gen. 10:8; 1 Chr. 1:10). From him the land of Cush seems to have derived its name. The question of the precise locality of the land of Cush has given rise to not a little controversy. The second river of Paradise surrounded the whole land of Cush (Gen. 2:13, R.V.). The term Cush is in the Old Testament generally applied to the countries south of the Israelites. It was the southern limit of Egypt (Ezek. 29:10, A.V.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
