derbe_330	Derbe	Derbe	Derbe	Derbe	\N	City	\N	37.348569	33.361453	Theographic	37.35092017	33.2714177	Unknown	Verified	\N	\N	\N	New Testament	4	Acts 14:20	A small town on the eastern part of the upland plain of Lycaonia, about 20 miles from Lystra. Paul passed through Derbe on his route from Cilicia to Iconium, on his second missionary journey (Acts 16:1), and probably also on his third journey (18:23; 19:1). On his first journey (14:20, 21) he came to Derbe from the other side; i.e., from Iconium. It was the native place of Gaius, one of Paul’s companions (20:4). He did not here suffer persecution (2 Tim. 3:11).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
