elath_366	Elath	Elath	Elath	Elath	\N	City	\N	29.528502	35.005732	Theographic	29.528502	35.005732	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	3	2 Kings 14:22	Grove; trees, (Deut. 2:8), also in plural form Eloth (1 Kings 9:26, etc.); called by the Greeks and Romans Elana; a city of Idumea, on the east, i.e., the Elanitic, gulf, or the Gulf of Akabah, of the Red Sea. It is first mentioned in Deut. 2:8. It is also mentioned along with Ezion-geber in 1 Kings 9:26. It was within the limits of Solomon’s dominion, but afterwards revolted. It was, however, recovered and held for a time under king Uzziah (2 Kings 14:22). Now the ruin Aila.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
