gederah_452	Gederah	Gederah	Gederah	Gederah	\N	City	\N	31.823337	34.777779	Theographic	31.823337	34.777779	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	3	1 Chronicles 12:4	The fortress; a fortified place, a town in the plain (shephelah) of Judah (Josh. 15:36). This is a very common Canaanite and Phoenician name. It is the feminine form of Geder (12:13); the plural form is Gederoth (15:41). This place has by some been identified with Jedireh, a ruin 9 miles from Lydda, toward Eleutheropolis, and 4 miles north of Sur’ah (Zorah), in the valley of Elah.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
