gibeon_470	Gibeon	Gibeon	Gibeon	Gibeon	\N	City	\N	31.84668	35.1852	Theographic	31.84684773	35.18491238	Unknown	Verified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	35	1 Chronicles 12:4	Hill-city, “one of the royal cities, greater than Ai, and all the men thereof were mighty” (Josh. 10:2). Its inhabitants were Hivites (11:19). It lay within the territory of Benjamin, and became a priest-city (18:25; 21:17). Here the tabernacle was set up after the destruction of Nob, and here it remained many years till the temple was built by Solomon. It is represented by the modern el-Jib, to the south-west of Ai, and about 5 1/2 miles north-north-west of Jerusalem.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
