gilo_478	Gilo	Gilo	Gilo	Gilo	\N	Unknown	\N	31.616667	35.083333	Theographic	31.616667	35.083333	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	1	2 Samuel 23:34	A name given to Hashem, an inhabitant of Gizoh, a place somewhere in the mountains of Judah (1 Chr. 11:34; 2 Sam. 23:32, 34).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
giloh_479	Giloh	Giloh	Giloh	Giloh	\N	City	\N	31.616667	35.083333	Theographic	31.616667	35.083333	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	2	2 Samuel 15:12	Exile, a city in the south-west part of the hill-country of Judah (Josh. 15:51). It was the native place or residence of the traitor Ahithophel “the Gilonite” (Josh. 15:51; 2 Sam. 15:12), and where he committed suicide (17:23). It has been identified with Kurbet Jala, about 7 miles north of Hebron.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
gimzo_480	Gimzo	Gimzo	Gimzo	Gimzo	\N	City	\N	31.928659	34.943219	Theographic	31.928659	34.943219	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	1	2 Chronicles 28:18	A place fertile in sycamores, a city in the plain of Judah, the villages of which were seized by the Philistines (2 Chr. 28:18). It is now called Jimzu, about 3 miles south-east of Ludd, i.e., Lydda.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
