ham_514	Ham	Ham (region, Genesis 14:5)	Ham	Ham	\N	Region	\N	31.95018855	35.92413136	Theographic	31.95018855	35.92413136	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	1	Genesis 14:5	Warm, hot, and hence the south; also an Egyptian word meaning “black”, the youngest son of Noah (Gen. 5:32; comp. 9:22, 24). The curse pronounced by Noah against Ham, properly against Canaan his fourth son, was accomplished when the Jews subsequently exterminated the Canaanites. One of the most important facts recorded in Gen. 10 is the foundation of the earliest monarchy in Babylonia by Nimrod the grandson of Ham (6, 8, 10).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
