haran_527	Haran	Haran	Haran	Haran	\N	City	\N	36.86	39.03139	Theographic	36.86386408	39.03219672	Unknown	Verified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	10	2 Kings 19:12	Heb. haran, i.e., “parched;” or probably from the Accadian charana, meaning “a road.” A celebrated city of Western Asia, now Harran, where Abram remained, after he left Ur of the Chaldees, till his father Terah died (Gen. 11:31, 32), when he continued his journey into the land of Canaan. It is called “Charran” in the LXX. and in Acts 7:2. It is called the “city of Nahor” (Gen. 24:10), and Jacob resided here with Laban (30:43).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
