mahaneh-dan_757	Mahaneh-dan	Mahaneh-dan	Mahaneh-dan	Mahaneh-dan	\N	Unknown	\N	31.758315	34.994252	Theographic	31.758315	34.994252	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	2	Judges 13:25	Judg. 18:12 = “camp of Dan” 13:25 (R.V., “Mahaneh-dan”), a place behind (i.e., west of) Kirjath-jearim, where the six hundred Danites from Zorah and Eshtaol encamped on their way to capture the city of Laish, which they rebuilt and called “Dan, after the name of their father” (18:11-31). The Palestine Explorers point to a ruin called ‘Erma, situated about 3 miles from the great corn valley on the east of Samson’s home.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
