michmas_792	Michmas	Michmas	Michmas	Michmas	\N	City	\N	31.87018434	35.27923582	Theographic	31.87018434	35.27923582	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	2	Ezra 2:27	Something hidden, a town of Benjamin (Ezra 2:27), east of Bethel and south of Migron, on the road to Jerusalem (Isa. 10:28). It lay on the line of march of an invading army from the north, on the north side of the steep and precipitous Wady es-Suweinit (“valley of the little thorn-tree” or “the acacia”), and now bears the name of Mukhmas. This wady is called “the passage of Michmash” (1 Sam. 13:23).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
