midian_796	Midian	Midian	Midian	Midian	\N	Region	\N	28.75	34.75	Theographic	28.932881	34.90832	Related-Surrounding	Verified	\N	\N	region	Old Testament	44	1 Chronicles 1:46	An Arabian tribe descended from Midian. They inhabited principally the desert north of the peninsula of Arabia. The peninsula of Sinai was the pasture-ground for their flocks. They were virtually the rulers of Arabia, being the dominant tribe. Like all Arabians, they were a nomad people. They early engaged in commercial pursuits. It was to one of their caravans that Joseph was sold (Gen. 37:28, 36).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
