paran_921	Paran	Paran	Paran	Paran	\N	Unknown	\N	28.717525	33.609633	Theographic	29.151667	33.541944	Rough	Verified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	8	1 Kings 11:18	Abounding in foliage, or abounding in caverns, (Gen. 21:21), a desert tract forming the north-eastern division of the peninsula of Sinai, lying between the ‘Arabah on the east and the wilderness of Shur on the west. It is intersected in a north-western direction by the Wady el-‘Arish. It bears the modern name of Badiet et-Tih, i.e., “the desert of the wanderings.” This district, through which the children of Israel wandered, lay three days’ march from Sinai (Num. 10:12, 33).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
