pavement_1155	Pavement	Pavement	Pavement	The Stone Pavement	\N	Landmark	\N	31.777444	35.234935	Theographic	31.777444	35.234935	Related-Within	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	New Testament	1	John 19:13	It was the custom of the Roman governors to erect their tribunals in open places, as the market-place, the circus, or even the highway. Pilate caused his seat of judgment to be set down in a place called “the Pavement” (John 19:13) i.e., a place paved with a mosaic of coloured stones. It was probably a place thus prepared in front of the “judgment hall.”	Easton's Bible Dictionary
