pisgah_950	Pisgah	Pisgah	Pisgah	Pisgah	\N	Unknown	\N	31.7650313	35.71856576	Theographic	31.7650313	35.71856576	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	5	Deuteronomy 3:27	A part, a mountain summit in the land of Moab, in the territory of Reuben, where Balak offered up sacrifices (Num. 21:20; 23:14), and from which Moses viewed the promised land (Deut. 3:27). It is probably the modern Jebel Siaghah.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
