pisidia_952	Pisidia	Pisidia	Pisidia	Pisidia	\N	Region	\N	37.25	30.75	Theographic	38.31643056393041	31.17948683048973	Rough	Verified	\N	\N	\N	New Testament	2	Acts 13:14	A district in Asia Minor, to the north of Pamphylia. The Taurus range of mountains extends through it. Antioch, one of its chief cities, was twice visited by Paul (Acts 13:14; 14:21-24).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
pithom_953	Pithom	Pithom	Pithom	Pithom	\N	City	\N	30.59385133	32.18555803	Theographic	30.59385133	32.18555803	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	1	Exodus 1:11	Egyptian, Pa-Tum, “house of Tum,” the sun-god, one of the “treasure” cities built for Pharaoh Rameses II. by the Israelites (Ex. 1:11). It was probably the Patumos of the Greek historian Herodotus. It has now been satisfactorily identified with Tell-el-Maskhuta, about 12 miles west of Ismailia, and 20 east of Tel-el-Kebir, on the southern bank of the present Suez Canal.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
