ramah_972	Ramah	Ramah (city, 1 Kings 15:17)	Ramah	Ramah	\N	City	\N	31.89964	35.20422	Theographic	31.89637864	35.20173069	Unknown	Verified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	17	1 Kings 15:17	A city first mentioned in Josh. 18:25, near Gibeah of Benjamin. It was fortified by Baasha, king of Israel (1 Kings 15:17-22; 2 Chr. 16:1-6). Asa, king of Judah, employed Benhadad the Syrian king to drive Baasha from this city (1 Kings 15:18, 20). Isaiah (10:29) refers to it, and also Jeremiah, who was once a prisoner there among the other captives of Jerusalem when it was taken by Nebuchadnezzar (Jer. 39:8-12; 40:1).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
