shiloh_1081	Shiloh	Shiloh	Shiloh	Shiloh	\N	City	\N	32.05617	35.28988	Theographic	32.05570051	35.2895287	Unknown	Verified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	30	1 Kings 14:2	Generally understood as denoting the Messiah, “the peaceful one,” as the word signifies (Gen. 49:10). The Vulgate Version translates the word, “he who is to be sent,” in allusion to the Messiah; the Revised Version, margin, “till he come to Shiloh;” and the LXX., “until that which is his shall come to Shiloh.” It is most simple and natural to render the expression, as in the Authorized Version, “till Shiloh come,” interpreting it as a proper name (comp. Isa. 9:6).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
shimron_1082	Shimron	Shimron	Shimron	Shimron	\N	City	\N	32.70528896	35.21333286	Theographic	32.70528896	35.21333286	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	2	Joshua 11:1	Watch-post, an ancient city of the Canaanites; with its villages, allotted to Zebulun (Josh. 19:15); now probably Semunieh, on the northern edge of the plain of Esdraelon, 5 miles west of Nazareth.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
