shittim_1086	Shittim	Shittim	Shittim	Shittim	\N	Unknown	\N	31.85826218	35.64156653	Theographic	31.85826218	35.64156653	Unknown	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	4	Joshua 2:1	Acacias, also called “Abel-shittim” (Num. 33:49), a plain or valley in the land of Moab where the Israelites were encamped after their two victories over Sihon and Og, at the close of their desert wanderings, and from which Joshua sent forth two spies (q.v.) “secretly” to “view” the land and Jericho (Josh. 2:1).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
shoa_1087	Shoa	Shoa	Shoa	Shoa	\N	Region	\N	34.798311	48.514966	Theographic	34.798311	48.514966	Rough	Unverified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	1	Ezekiel 23:23	Opulent, the mountain district lying to the north-east of Babylonia, anciently the land of the Guti, or Kuti, the modern Kurdistan. The plain lying between these mountains and the Tigris was called su-Edina, i.e., “the border of the plain.” This name was sometimes shortened into Suti and Su, and has been regarded as = Shoa (Ezek. 23:23). Some think it denotes a place in Babylon.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
