sodom_1107	Sodom	Sodom	Sodom	Sodom	\N	City	\N	31.19656033	35.39648412	Theographic	31.19656033	35.39648412	Unknown	Not identifiable	\N	\N	\N	Both	47	2 Peter 2:6	Burning; the walled, a city in the vale of Siddim (Gen. 13:10; 14:1-16). The wickedness of its inhabitants brought down upon it fire from heaven, by which it was destroyed (18:16-33; 19:1-29; Deut. 23:17). This city and its awful destruction are frequently alluded to in Scripture (Deut. 29:23; 32:32; Isa. 1:9, 10; 3:9; 13:19; Jer. 23:14; Ezek. 16:46-56; Zeph. 2:9; Matt. 10:15; Rom. 9:29; 2 Pet. 2:6, etc.).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
solomons_portico_1109	Solomon's Portico	Solomon's Portico	Solomon's Portico	Solomon's Portico	Solomon's Porch	Landmark	\N	31.777444	35.234935	Theographic	31.777444	35.234935	Related-Within	Not identifiable	\N	\N	\N	New Testament	2	Acts 3:11	(John 10:23; Acts 3:11; 5:12), a colonnade, or cloister probably, on the eastern side of the temple. It is not mentioned in connection with the first temple, but Josephus mentions a porch, so called, in Herod’s temple (q.v.).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
