tabor_1128	Tabor (Mountain)	Tabor (Mountain)	Tabor	Tabor	\N	Mountain	\N	32.687114	35.390383	Theographic	32.6869564	35.39091304	Unknown	Verified	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	5	Hosea 5:1	Now Jebel et-Tur, a cone-like prominent mountain, 11 miles west of the Sea of Galilee. It is about 1,843 feet high. The view from the summit of it is said to be singularly extensive and grand. This is alluded to in Ps. 89:12; Jer. 46:18. It was here that Barak encamped before the battle with Sisera (q.v.) Judg. 4:6-14. There is an old tradition, which, however, is unfounded, that it was the scene of the transfiguration of our Lord.	Easton's Bible Dictionary
