zion_1263	Zion	Zion	Zion	Zion	\N	Mountain	\N	31.776667	35.234167	Theographic	31.777444	35.234935	Precise	Verified	\N	\N	Same as Jerusalem	Both	140	1 Chronicles 11:5	Sunny; height, one of the eminences on which Jerusalem was built. It was surrounded on all sides, except the north, by deep valleys, that of the Tyropoeon (q.v.) separating it from Moriah (q.v.), which it surpasses in height by 105 feet. It was the south-eastern hill of Jerusalem. When David took it from the Jebusites (Josh. 15:63; 2 Sam. 5:7) he built on it a citadel and a palace, and it became “the city of David” (1 Kings 8:1; 2 Kings 19:21, 31; 1 Chr. 11:5).	Easton's Bible Dictionary
